// Words that do not follow their tongue's sound rules, each with its reason.
// Read by src/names/mod.rs. An entry here wins over the rules.
//
//   root    the root's English key (roots.ron)
//   tongue  the tongue the exception is in
//   form    the word as it really is
//   why     the reason
[
    (root: "death", tongue: Roduro, form: "ṭeyuʻoye", why: "Canon. The Roduro word is far longer than a root: the other tongues keep only the root's first part (ṭeyu), and Roduro's long form is taken as it stands."),
    (root: "migrate", tongue: Tadoro, form: "shetha", why: "The rules give shitha, which reads badly in English (avoid.ron). The vowel is opened; nothing else changes."),
]
